{"name":"Fierce Mantis","hex":"#7fc15c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fierce","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Exceedingly violent, severe, ferocious, cruel or savage.","Resolute or strenuously active."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Extremely; very."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fierce"},{"term":"mantis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various large insects of the order Mantodea that catch insects or other small animals with their powerful forelegs.","A green colour, like that of many mantises. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mantis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fierce","blocks":[{"text":"Fierce were a British three-piece, all girl R&B group. They were signed to Colin Lester and Ian McAndrew's Wildstar Records, and scored four hit singles on the UK Singles Chart in 1999 and 2000. The biggest of the hits, \"Sweet Love 2K\", is a cover of the Anita Baker song \"Sweet Love\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fierce","wikidata":"Q5447265"},{"title":"Mantis","blocks":[{"text":"Mantises are an order (Mantodea) of insects that contains over 2,400 species in about 460 genera in 33 families. The largest family is the Mantidae (\"mantids\"). Mantises are distributed worldwide in temperate and tropical habitats. They have triangular heads with bulging eyes supported on flexible necks. Their elongated bodies may or may not have wings, but all mantodeans have forelegs that are greatly enlarged and adapted for catching and gripping prey; their upright posture, while remaining stationary with forearms folded, resembling a praying posture, has led to the common name praying mantis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Mantis_%28European%29.jpg/330px-Mantis_%28European%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis","wikidata":"Q131250"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/500px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/1280px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/500px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stagmomantis carolina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Santanmantis_reconstruction.png/500px-Santanmantis_reconstruction.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Santanmantis_reconstruction.png/1280px-Santanmantis_reconstruction.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Santanmantis_reconstruction.png/500px-Santanmantis_reconstruction.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c